SM(306,{"n":"Exodus 24.1-11","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Exodus 24.1-11.mp3","d":2531.2,"s":[[0.24,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.96,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in biblical studies, and it's an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[20.88,"Okay, we'll go ahead and get started."],[22.64,"We're gonna get started here in just a moment."],[25.44,"We're gonna be picking up at the beginning of Exodus chapter 24."],[33.76,"We've been we're still in sort of um what's a good way to describe this?"],[42.0,"So the covenant has been given at Mount Sinai to Israel."],[46.16,"We're about to start getting, we may get into that tonight."],[50.0,"I'm not good at predicting those sort of things, as everyone who listens to this knows."],[54.96,"Um we may get into this tonight."],[57.04,"The instructions for building the tabernacle."],[59.72,"And the building of the tabernacle is going to take up most of the rest of the book of Exodus."],[66.44,"And so we're sort of in this intermediate period."],[68.84,"A lot of what we read last time was chapter 20, we got the Ten Commandments."],[77.42,"The ten words."],[78.62,"And then a lot of the material we've been reading since then has been sort of expansions on different commandments in the sense of, okay, so what does it mean to honor the Sabbath day?"],[89.74,"What does it mean to not bear false witness?"],[93.02,"What does it."],[93.64,"And sort of breaking that down in sort of real sometimes really practical terms."],[99.41,"What does it mean to not steal?"],[100.93,"What does it mean to not?"],[102.21,"What are some different ways you could break that commandment of stealing?"],[103.73,"You know, aside from just obviously this belonged to someone else that I took it, right"],[110.89,"That there are other ways in which you can violate that."],[114.97,"Uh right at the end of last time, uh, we talked a little bit."],[120.41,"Uh God was telling Moses about the angel of the Lord, the angel who God had placed his name in, who he talked about as the second person of the Trinity."],[130.73,"Uh, short version."],[132.97,"Uh, because again, we're not gonna go through that again."],[136.01,"This is Christ in the Old Testament."],[139.21,"Uh that this angel, even though he's not always gonna be quote unquote on camera as we go through the rest of the Torah, uh, and even. Joshua, is there and will appear at various points on camera"],[154.69,"Not that he's like invisible and appears and disappears, but will you know be spoken of directly in the text at several points."],[160.85,"And then when we get into the book of Judges, at the beginning of the book of Judges, he will speak to the people of Israel and then leave."],[169.81,"So there's this period of time beginning with what we just read and ending at the beginning of Judges."],[175.57,"This period of well over 40 years where the angel of the Lord is living encamped with the people of Israel."],[185.27,"And leading them and is part of their experience of God."],[191.39,"Uh and so then the very end of what we read last time was talking about the angel of the Lord leading them in particular into the land at the end of this journey and helping them defeat the listed giant clans that we talked about last time."],[210.91,"So that's where we left off."],[213.39,"And now we've got chapter 24, which is going to be some material that comes in between where we just left off and before in chapter 25, the tabernacle instructions and building begins."],[227.55,"So that's sort of where we are in the grand scheme of the book of Exodus."],[233.95,"So unless anybody has any leftover comments or questions or classic episodes of Twilight Zone they've liked to discuss, we'll go ahead and pick up in uh beginning of Exodus chapter 24."],[251.67,"Now he said to Moses, Come up to the Lord, you and Aaron, Nadab and Abahu, and seventy of the elders of Israel, and worship from afar."],[263.11,"Moses alone shall come near to God, but they shall not come near, nor shall the people go up with them."],[269.99,"Who is speaking?"],[271.51,"God. Yeah. That's why people hearing the recording can't see this, but in the Orthodox Study Bible, the H is capitalized."],[278.87,"So God says to Moses to come and to bring Aaron, his two oldest sons, Nadab and Abu, and the elders."],[287.05,"70 elders. Partway up the mountain."],[291.79,"Because there's top of the mountain to see God."],[294.59,"Only Moses is allowed up there."],[297.15,"People aren't allowed on the mountain at all."],[300.4,"But the elders and the chief priest and his two oldest sons, the two senior priests, they're gonna go partway up."],[308.0,"So remember how we've talked about part of what the Torah is doing with the commandments is establishing these sort of concentric circles."],[318.25,"So there's the Holy of Holies, there's a place where God is."],[322.62,"In uh the tabernacle."],[324.58,"Then there's the Holy. place in the tabernacle where just the priests go to offer incense"],[332.58,"Then there's sort of the courts of the tabernacle where the priests and the Levites go."],[337.22,"Then there's the camp, which is just the Israelites, and then there's outside the camp."],[342.47,"And you have to maintain a different level of holiness, sort of the closer you're going to go in."],[350.39,"So we're going to read when we get into Leviticus: only the high priest is going to be allowed to go into the most holy place, only one day a year, and he's going to have to do a whole bunch of things so that he could do that safely and not die."],[363.85,"And the priests, when it comes their time to serve and they go into the holy place, they're going to have ritual washings they're gonna do, they're gonna have to abstain from things during that period of time."],[376.07,"In terms of fasting and things."],[377.68,"They're gonna have to maintain this higher level of holiness during the time that they're going in there."],[382.1,"And the priests and the Levites in general are going to have to have a higher level than the regular quote unquote lay people, of Israel."],[391.24,"And the Israelites are gonna have to maintain a higher are supposed to maintain a higher level of holiness than all the people outside Israel."],[400.26,"Because they're God's people and God is dwelling with them."],[403.43,"And so this is part of the beginning of establishing that."],[407.36,"So we see this already here at Mount Sinai."],[410.24,"Tabernacle hasn't been built. yet"],[412.12,"God is up at the top of the mountain."],[413.98,"So the top of the mountain where God is, that's the most holy place."],[417.52,"That's the Holy of Holies right now."],[420.02,"And so the priests of the elders can come near to that, but not there."],[428.68,"They can't go into it."],[429.72,"Only Moses could go into it."],[431.4,"But they could come near."],[433.84,"And sort of the laity, the rest of the people, stay down at the bottom of the mountain."],[441.22,"And so this idea is being shown them on the mountain."],[446.78,"As we get into the instructions for building the tabernacle."],[451.11,"This sort of system of concentric circles is going to be made mobile."],[453.19,"In the camp as they're going to pick up and move"],[458.33,"And then eventually, when they settle in the land, there's going to be the temple."],[463.79,"But it's still, there's still going to be this sense."],[465.8,"There's going to be a most holy place in the temple and a holy place, and then the courts, and then right, the rest of the land, and then outside of Israel."],[473.74,"The nations. Verse 3 So Moses came and told the people all the words of God and all the ordinances."],[489.5,"And all the people answered with one voice and said, All the words the Lord spoke, we will do."],[496.72,"So they had good intentions at the time."],[501.52,"Then Moses wrote all the words of the Lord, and he rose early in the morning and built an altar at the foot of the mountain, and twelve stones according to the twelve tribes of Israel."],[515.28,"So something to notice here."],[519.81,"So there's the tablets, remember?"],[524.13,"That God writes on, in terms of the covenant."],[527.67,"That we already talked about."],[530.43,"That had the Ten Commandments, basically."],[533.57,"The sort of summary."],[536.45,"But now it says, Moses wrote. all the words that God had said"],[543.77,"So what is that?"],[545.37,"Well, that's all these other things."],[547.83,"That we've been that we've been reading."],[550.57,"And we've already seen this."],[552.09,"We've already seen this."],[553.05,"So this is calling us back to that."],[555.53,"That it's not just, Moses is not just taking dictation."],[563.5,"But Moses is invested with the authority to take what God is revealing to him and to apply it to the people."],[574.78,"And part of that authority is the authority to put that in writing"],[581.99,"That it's not just Moses, while he's alive, has the authority to sort of adjudicate these things."],[589.61,"And then once he dies, someone else will adjudicate things."],[592.57,"But once he's gone, whatever Moses said kind of won't matter."],[597.03,"So part of his authority is the authority to write these things, what is going to become the actual Torah in our Bible."],[605.17,"To write these things for future generations."],[608.45,"So the authority of Moses isn't just while Moses is alive."],[611.41,"The authority given to Moses is the authority of Moses."],[615.75,"And we'll continue."],[618.0,"And so we'll get to a point at the other end of the Torah when Moses is approaching. his death, when he'll lay hands on Joshua and pass authority to him"],[628.36,"And when we get there, we'll talk more about what part of his authority or what elements of his authority or what kind of authority he's passing on to Joshua and what kind is unique to Moses."],[640.12,"We'll talk more about that then."],[643.0,"But if you're not making the connection already in your heads, the reason I'm sort of pointing this out and pointing to this is this is crucial to how we understand what's going on in the New Testament when we see the apostles' writing."],[660.1,"That the authority that Jesus gave to the apostles was not just, okay, while you're alive, you guys are in charge."],[668.68,"And then when you die, somebody else will be in charge."],[671.66,"It's not just like a bureaucratic structure of the church."],[674.94,"But apostolic authority was this sort of unique thing."],[679.44,"And part of that was them not just, well, I'm going to help the church in Corinth with some stuff they're dealing with, but I'm going to write letters to the church in Corinth dealing with that stuff that are going to be scripture."],[693.44,"That are going to be handed down for generations."],[697.8,"And they're going to be the basis for the people who come after."],[702.06,"Just like the people who came after Mo come after Moses, who had hands laid on them, are going to take the Torah from Moses and apply it, and use it."],[711.36,"The people who the apostles are going to set up as their successors are not going to keep writing Bible."],[718.66,"But they're going to take the apostolic writings and the other scriptures, and they're going to apply and interpret them in the succeeding generations."],[740.14,"The Torah relating to Moses and Moses' successors and what Moses writes."],[748.62,"That's sort of the pattern in terms of how that's understood."],[755.5,"And then he also builds this altar."],[758.4,"And he builds an altar of twelve stones, each one, because there's twelve tribes, that make up Israel."],[767.69,"Then he sent young men of the children of Israel who offered whole burnt offerings and sacrificed peace offerings of calves to God."],[775.37,"Moses took half the blood and put it in basins, and half the blood he poured on the altar."],[781.45,"Then he took the book of the covenant and read in the hearing of the people."],[786.73,"And they said, All the Lord said we will do and be obedient."],[790.57,"Moses then took the blood, sprinkled it on the people, and said, This is the blood of the covenant the Lord made with you, according to all these words."],[798.49,"So he does this ritual"],[803.01,"Now we haven't seen this ritual set out anywhere."],[808.71,"We're gonna get instructions for sacrifices and what to do with the blood and all that stuff in Leviticus."],[813.19,"You're gonna have a great time."],[817.27,"It's gonna be cool."],[818.07,"It's gonna go on for weeks."],[819.27,"You're gonna love Bible study."],[820.79,"Anyway. So he's gonna get all those instructions detailed, but we didn't we didn't see at least, we're not told anywhere that God gave Moses these detailed instructions to do this, even how to do the sacrifices, even how to build the altar or where to build the altar."],[837.88,"Now we can see he builds the altar with the twelve stones."],[840.68,"That's after the pattern of, remember, Jacob. built an altar like that"],[846.48,"Right? So it's following a pattern that's in Genesis."],[850.74,"But he's making offerings, and there's not a see the high priest, Moses?"],[859.86,"No, that's gonna be Aaron, but it's not even Aaron yet."],[863.12,"So what we see is the pattern that he's following is the pattern from Abraham, Isaac, Jacob in Genesis, still."],[873.29,"So as we get into the tabernacle being built, there's gonna be Aaron's priesthood is gonna be a set."],[879.13,"All these things haven't happened yet."],[881.31,"So we're still functioning at this point in the world that we were in. in Genesis"],[887.73,"This is we're sort of in media race here."],[891.75,"In the yes, sir."],[893.75,"These 12 pillars are these?"],[895.59,"Are like akin to like the standing stones?"],[899.27,"No, this is just an altar."],[901.19,"So for sacrificing."],[903.83,"What's the pillars?"],[905.35,"Which pillars? And he rose early in the morning and built an altar at the foot of the mountain in twelve pillars according to the."],[912.23,"It's twelve stones."],[913.43,"So it's not like the standing stones."],[914.87,"That's a tri no."],[916.63,"No, that's a translation thing."],[918.15,"Oh, yeah. It's an altar made of twelve stones."],[920.47,"Yeah. Um. And so the blood is going to be poured out when we get the instructions, but he saves half of it."],[929.99,"it. And he throws on the people"],[933.95,"You're very glad that I use water and not blood now, huh?"],[940.83,"But you'd still be okay, even in the old covenant, because this is one of the very rare occasions where blood is thrown on people."],[950.91,"Blood is almost never applied to people."],[956.83,"In uh in the Torah."],[960.19,"Did y'all already know from one of the priests?"],[962.03,"It might be."],[962.99,"That's later on."],[963.87,"We still haven't had the priesthood set up yet."],[965.95,"That's one of the other times."],[967.23,"So that''ss what it."],[968.03,"There's a couple of times."],[968.83,"There's here. This is a singular event."],[971.15,"This isn't something that happens over and over again."],[974.35,"Um there's the ordination of the high priest, where blood gets put on their right earlobe, their right thumb, and their right big toe."],[986.39,"Which we'll talk about more when we get there."],[989.99,"Um trying to think if there's a third time."],[995.27,"I think that is it."],[998.23,"When blood is actually applied to people."],[1001.27,"Uh I won't at this point delve too far into how problematic that is for certain people's views of the atonement."],[1013.51,"Um blood is always otherwise poured out, or on the Day of Atonement, it's applied to. to inanimate objects to purify them, not people"],[1028.27,"So, yeah. I think we talked about that back in Hebrews, actually, when we were talking about where the book of Hebrews says, without the shedding of blood, there is no remission of sins, and how the usual interpretation of that doesn't make any sense with the Torah."],[1041.95,"Um, but uh yeah, so this is our this is a rare occasion."],[1051.6,"Uh most people in the history of Israel never had any blood thrown at them or applied to them."],[1057.36,"99.99999% of people."],[1061.6,"So are is this supposed to be? related to the same covenant type situation with Abraham"],[1070.28,"Like is this kind of like a new covenant?"],[1073.96,"Yes. Yes. So remember back when Abraham, when God made the covenant with Abraham, he had Abraham split the animals, the birds and animals split them in half and sort of butterfly them."],[1090.76,"And we talked about how normally, when someone was taking that kind of it was a an oath-taking ritual where you would walk between the halves and then say, if I violate this covenant, may I end up like these animals?"],[1111.13,"Split in half."],[1112.73,"And then the thing that happens in Genesis is that it's the presence of God that looks like a fiery torch that moves between the halves."],[1121.77,"Where you would be expecting God to make Abraham walk between the halves."],[1127.87,"To say that he's going to keep God's covenant."],[1131.39,"God walks between them and says, if I don't keep my promises to you, Abraham, then may I end up, like these, uh like these animals."],[1141.77,"But it's that's related to oath-taking."],[1145.35,"And that's what's going on here."],[1147.05,"Because the people are taking an oath."],[1149.45,"People are saying, oh yeah, all that stuff, yeah, we're on board, we're gonna do all those things or not do all those things you told us not to do."],[1160.17,"We got this."],[1162.62,"And so they then have the blood of that sacrifice, which was offered to God, thrown on them to sort of seal, seal the deal, as it were."],[1175.99,"That okay, you have agreed to it."],[1178.4,"And implied in there with shed blood is the consequence of violating this."],[1187.26,"This is a witness to what you swore."],[1191.47,"This blood will be a witness against. you if now you go and violate the covenant"],[1198.07,"The last thing uh this is the blood of the covenant."],[1202.31,"Obviously, it looks somewhat similar to this."],[1204.71,"Yes. You're tracking with me."],[1206.47,"Yes. That's where I'm going."],[1208.15,"Okay. So we come to the New Testament."],[1215.24,"And we'll talk specifically about, because St."],[1218.2,"Matthew helps us in his gospel by making a special point of this."],[1223.42,"Matthew, Mark, and Luke all describe the mystical supper or the Last Supper in Christ instituting the Eucharist."],[1231.5,"St. John's Gospel doesn't."],[1233.58,"The fourth place you find it in the New Testament is actually in 1 Corinthians, where St."],[1236.7,"About St Paul describes it."],[1240.74,"Matthew, because it's going to be followed up on by him later to make the point very clear."],[1246.99,"Christ says, referring to the cup that he blesses."],[1250.05,"This is my blood of the new covenant."],[1254.71,"Which is shed for you and for many."],[1256.95,"So we have this sacrifice that initiates the Mosaic covenant."],[1265.64,"Later in the Hebrew scriptures in the Old Testament, in Jeremiah and Ezekiel, and a few other places, Jeremiah 31, and a couple other places are sort of the uh classical places."],[1281.44,"Look for it, it refers to there being a new covenant with Israel in the latter days."],[1287.28,"And we've talked before about like the Greek word caney that we read as new."],[1294.37,"How that's not new in the sense that we tend to think about it."],[1299.17,"When we hear new, we think, oh, this is new, it's never existed before."],[1305.02,"It's all new, it's different."],[1306.88,"It's all new, all different."],[1309.12,"Nothing like this has ever been around before."],[1312.21,"Um, whereas uh Canyan Greek, uh the idea here is more of renewed."],[1320.05,"renewed. It's new and it's fresh, but that's because it's been and refreshed"],[1328.15,"Um it doesn't mean never existed before, now exists."],[1333.32,"And part of where we see that, I think the last time I talked about this was when we were in 1 John."],[1338.92,"And St. John says, a new commandment I give to you to love one another."],[1342.6,"And it's like, what are you talking about, new?"],[1346.68,"Like, that's all through, like, not just all through the New Testament, that's all through the Bible."],[1351.89,"Like, that's we already we saw like love your enemies, like a chapter ago in Exodus."],[1356.31,"And St. John follows up by saying, but this is not a new commandment."],[1361.13,"This is what you've been taught from the beginning."],[1363.61,"And so then what does it mean when he says I'm giving you a new commandment"],[1368.03,"It means he's renewing that commandment to them."],[1374.4,"Saying, Let me remind you of this."],[1376.56,"Let me sort of refresh this in your mind."],[1380.29,"This is what you were called to do."],[1381.81,"This isn't something you've never heard before."],[1385.35,"But I'm giving it to you anew."],[1388.37,"And so the same is true of the new covenant."],[1392.67,"And if you read even briefly, so for example, Jeremiah 31, that's Jeremiah 31 in the Hebrew version."],[1402.19,"I don't have my Jeremiah chart in front of me."],[1405.15,"So, you know, figure it out if you have a problem with that"],[1411.75,"Because it is in the Greek version, but the Greek version is completely rearranged from the Hebrew version."],[1418.63,"More about that when we get to the book of Jeremiah."],[1421.91,"One of the first things it says about the new covenant is that God will write the Torah on people's hearts."],[1430.55,"Well, the Torah is the quote unquote old covenant."],[1437.51,"So if the new covenant involves him writing the old covenant on people's hearts, is it really new?"],[1444.47,"In the sense of completely different?"],[1446.63,"Now we can throw out the old one because we have the new one?"],[1449.27,"Well, no, obviously not."],[1451.92,"If the new one is the old one being written on your heart, then that means it's renewed, it's refreshed, it's transformed, but it's still the same thing."],[1465.08,"And so when Christ talks about the new covenant being made in his blood, number one, he's talking about that new covenant that was prophesied in the latter days."],[1476.97,"Talking about this is now the covenant being renewed, the sacrifice that is going to happen."],[1485.19,"Sacrifice that's going to happen to initiate that covenant, like the sacrifice that happened here to initiate this one, is Christ's sacrifice, Christ's self-offing."],[1493.03,"That's the sacrifice"],[1498.97,"And the people who were there when this covenant with Moses was initiated."],[1506.89,"The people who are there vowed to keep it."],[1512.67,"And then were sprinkled with the blood."],[1516.35,"And that's how they became participants."],[1520.99,"And so Christ is saying, that is the blood of the new covenant."],[1527.51,"Then when you eat Christ's flesh and drink Christ's blood, a law, John chapter 6."],[1536.81,"Then you become a participant in the new covenant."],[1543.9,"And this is why part of what's going on when we receive the Eucharist, when we celebrate the Eucharist together, is us renewing this kind of vow to Christ."],[1558.62,"And it's got to be renewed a lot because we mess up."],[1561.96,"That's all that you say we will do."],[1566.57,"Recommitting to following him."],[1572.33,"Not standing up and professing that we've done that perfectly, but renewing our commitment to do that."],[1578.97,"And we have to remember that then"],[1586.37,"The reason I chose to talk about St."],[1587.97,"Matthew's gospel in particular is that it's not long after Jesus says that that a big crowd of people says, Let his blood be on us and on our children."],[1601.65,"By which they don't mean Jewish people who may or may not be biologically descended from that crowd are guilty of Jesus' death for the rest of eternity."],[1614.29,"That is not what that means."],[1616.93,"This is an example of, this is something that the gospels do all the time"],[1621.46,"They have somebody say something and they don't realize. what they're really saying"],[1625.5,"Like remember Caiaphas the high priest says about Jesus, well, it's good for one man to die, like to save the people."],[1633.02,"And he means from the Romans."],[1635.04,"He means Jesus is causing trouble, so we're going to kill him to get the Romans off our backs."],[1638.56,"That's what he meant."],[1640.46,"But the words he said meant something far more profound than he realized."],[1646.32,"So St. Matthew's doing the same kind of thing."],[1648.48,"This crowd just wants to see Jesus dead."],[1650.64,"That's how they attend it."],[1653.89,"But they say something, something far more profound."],[1660.09,"In that what they're really saying is that they want to be part of this new covenant."],[1667.73,"So that would almost be another time when blood is supplied to people."],[1671.71,"And that's that language."],[1672.91,"Is blood be on us?"],[1674.45,"That's clearly a reference back to this idea."],[1678.15,"Even though that's not how they meant it at the time."],[1682.77,"And this is part of a pattern."],[1684.54,"What St. Matthew is using this."],[1688.8,"He's trying to show us that, yes, what we're reading about from one perspective, what we're reading about in St."],[1696.88,"Matthew's Gospel is the murder of Jesus, who was innocent."],[1702.58,"And who was executed in this horrible, hideous way."],[1707.08,"From one level."],[1708.2,"But what St."],[1708.92,"Matthew wants to say about it is that God took that murder, this horrible evil that humans concocted."],[1718.86,"It did, and God turns that around and turns it into this great good."],[1726.31,"So it's not trying to put blame on anybody for the crime."],[1729.83,"It's trying to show how God turned that crime into a blessing for the Jewish people and for all the nations of the world."],[1737.83,"Well, it's either right"],[1739.19,"That's what St."],[1739.67,"Matthew's trying to say."],[1740.75,"'s more It it's even more interesting when you contrast that with what they say here, which is we're gonna do everything."],[1746.31,"Yeah. And we know you don't."],[1748.07,"Yeah. And so you have like this kind of especially this group."],[1749.99,"Yeah This group's all gonna die in the desert."],[1753.07,"And so you have the complete inverse of they don't mean their saying either."],[1759.71,"So it's just really it's almost yeah, it's almost one for one."],[1763.79,"Yeah. Yeah. But so this is the episode that Christ is alluding back to when he says that that St."],[1771.87,"Matthew is alluding back to."],[1776.24,"Um because blood doesn't get on put put on people otherwise."],[1781.14,"That's not a thing."],[1782.34,"It's not a thing that happens."],[1785.54,"Verse nine, after this, Moses went up along with Aaron, Nadab, and Abahu, and the seventy of the elders of Israel."],[1792.66,"of Israel. And they saw the place where the God stood"],[1797.42,"Under his feet was, as it were, a paved work of sapphire stone, and the appearance of heaven's firmament in its purity."],[1805.9,"So what's that saying is they see God standing on the sky."],[1811.98,"And of Israel's chosen men, not one was missing."],[1815.82,"So they saw the place of God and ate and drank."],[1821.02,"So they see God in human form, because look, he's got feet."],[1829.47,"This is another instance."],[1830.99,"So this is seventy or seventy-two elders plus Aaron plus Nadab plus Abahu."],[1838.03,"Right after And they have a meal there."],[1845.19,"They have a meal with God there."],[1848.47,"Right after this sacrifice and the blood of the covenant."],[1854.72,"Mystical supper. Do you see things coming together here?"],[1858.0,"Okay. Notice they eat and drink."],[1862.57,"So again, when Christ is eating the meal with his and he appeals back to this chapter, it's not for nothing."],[1871.21,"Let me add this too."],[1873.85,"Because there's something important here, too, that we might miss."],[1876.89,"If you don't know what's going to happen next."],[1880.27,"If you don't know what's going to happen in Leviticus."],[1881.31,"Leviticus Anybody know off the top of their head what's going to happen to Nadab and Abuhu and?"],[1881.71,"Yeah They're both dead in Leviticus."],[1893.67,"Two oldest sons of Aaron."],[1896.21,"He has two younger sons who are gonna end up being like Eliezer is gonna end up being high priest after him."],[1901.57,"He's not good, he doesn't get to go up the mountain and see God."],[1905.25,"Is Nadab and Abahu are gonna be dead."],[1909.73,"In Leviticus, I think it's chapter 9, 9 or 10."],[1913.75,"Which isn't that far in the future."],[1915.35,"If you take out the tabernacle instructions and tabernacle building, that's almost the next story."],[1921.15,"Right in the Torah."],[1923.23,"Okay, they're about to die."],[1926.83,"So why are they given this vision?"],[1931.81,"Like, could have just been Aaron, who's gonna be the high priest."],[1936.61,"Could have been Aaron and all four of his sons, like the two who are gonna live and actually be high priests."],[1944.45,"Why is it these two?"],[1946.93,"Why is it Jesus?"],[1949.09,"This is an important question."],[1952.86,"Notice I'm not saying the answer is important."],[1955.26,"The question is important."],[1958.7,"The question is important."],[1960.7,"Because this is a question that's gonna have echoes all through the rest of the scriptures, Old Testament and New Testament."],[1969.44,"Because there's going to be other versions of this question."],[1973.04,"For example, why does God bring 12 tribes out of Egypt and settle them in the land when 10 of them are going to go?"],[1989.33,"There's a big Old Testament example."],[1992.43,"Because he knows, it's not like he doesn't know what's going to happen."],[1999.4,"Well, let's have some New Testament examples."],[2002.76,"Here's a big New Testament example."],[2005.08,"As we read the Gospels, Christ has the twelve."],[2011.32,"So we have Judas is there."],[2011.88,"Judas So we've got."],[2012.12,"But even more so, he's got an inner circle of three"],[2018.19,"Saints Peter, James, and John."],[2019.87,"There are all these times like when Christ raises the dead, he goes off with Saints Peter, James, and John."],[2027.09,"Those three. When uh Transfiguration that we're about to celebrate as we record this."],[2035.55,"He goes to the top of the Mount of Transfiguration, goes up the mountain."],[2039.47,"You're gonna see his glory."],[2040.91,"It's Peter, James, John."],[2042.61,"There's this inner circle."],[2044.37,"Many more times he goes aside with them to pray."],[2047.73,"They're the ones who get sort of the inner circle."],[2051.22,"And then when we get to, say, Galatians, and we're talking about the early church."],[2057.18,"And St. Paul talks about the pillars of the early church."],[2061.66,"He says, well, it's say it's Peter, James, and John."],[2066.06,"He's talking about a different James."],[2070.78,"He's talking about James the Lord's brother."],[2074.54,"He's not talking about St."],[2075.58,"James the son of Zebedee, who was part of that inner circle who witnessed all those things."],[2079.1,"Because St. James the son of Zebedee got killed by Herod very early in the book of Acts."],[2084.14,"Never really got to be a leader in the church."],[2087.9,"So why was he in that inner circle?"],[2092.86,"Why not somebody else with the twelve?"],[2096.94,"Was it just because he had the same name as the guy who was later going to be?"],[2104.95,"So this is a question that's found just all through the scriptures."],[2112.31,"Where God chooses to give revelation of himself to some people and not to others."],[2122.39,"And at different levels to not an answer this question, other than God reveals Himself to different people at different times."],[2139.09,"Surely there could have been a better 12th guy than Judas."],[2141.73,"as. Thom or St"],[2144.01,"Surely St. Andrew or somebody who was going to live a little longer could have been in that inner circle."],[2152.49,"Surely there were some people on the earth who would have been at least as faithful as Judah and Benjamin were, because it's not like they were perfect."],[2164.41,"Who could have been called instead of those no good northern tribes."],[2169.31,"Who are disobedient."],[2174.15,"But so the fact that God knows how someone is going to react."],[2181.83,"If someone's going to react in a negative way, or someone is going to waste the light that God is going to give them, does not stop God from giving them that light."],[2193.11,"And he doesn't only reveal himself and only give that light to the people he knows are going to respond the right way, or the best."],[2205.75,"Or for whom he has some magnificent destiny, as we would see it from our perspective."],[2216.2,"That's just not how God works."],[2220.72,"And the reason it's important for us to remember this open question is we tend to ask this from a very different and often more selfish perspective."],[2234.0,"Like we tend to be more like when Saints James and John andor their mother go up to Jesus and say, hey, we want to be the right hand man and your left-hand man."],[2245.68,"We want to position authority."],[2247.44,"And all the other disciples are like, Yeah, anything they are."],[2251.58,"We tend to be more like them."],[2254.72,"Like, why did God give this to that person?"],[2257.68,"Why did God why didn't why hasn't God done that for me?"],[2260.72,"Why hasn't God, you know, why have it"],[2263.74,"We did ask it from a very sort of selfish kind of thing."],[2267.44,"And it's rarely, in terms of being self-centered, it's rarely, wow, why has God given me all these wonderful blessings I didn't deserve?"],[2273.6,"Which we should think more often"],[2278.84,"It tends to be more about all the ones we feel like we haven't been given, especially if we see them given to somebody else, especially if we see them given to somebody else who we don't like, or we think is wasting them, or we think we could do better, if only we had them."],[2299.7,"That't really think of this that if you did have such a blessing or revelation or something like that, it doesn't necessarily mean you shouldn't necessarily think that you you're sort of special and wonderful."],[2318.78,"Yes. Yes. Yeah."],[2323.58,"And I'm sure, yeah."],[2325.58,"I don't know that anybody in this room is that category, but there might be someone listening to this category who receives some blessing from God, receives some from God."],[2334.7,"Therefore, things. So, you know."],[2337.18,"Nadab and Abuhu had no reason as they were sitting there eating and drinking to think, oh, God loves me more than those people down at the foot of the mountain."],[2347.42,"Any more than they had a right to be jealous of Moses, who got to go further up."],[2353.31,"Um Yeah, so that's prone too."],[2357.39,"And that, and that idea is why the fathers always say, you, if you think you have a vision from God, if you think an angel has appeared to you, if you think this, this, this should always assume no."],[2370.71,"And if it's real, God will make it so real that you can't deny it."],[2376.41,"But until then, you should just doubt it."],[2379.29,"Because the other way lies pride getting puffed up."],[2384.99,"I'm the one God has chosen."],[2388.32,"All of this kind of thing."],[2389.52,"And that's why St."],[2390.32,"Paul, remember when St."],[2391.28,"Paul was talking about the thorn in his flesh and talking about all the hardships he endured."],[2395.86,"He understood in his head, he's like, yes, God called me to this very important ministry."],[2400.58,"I received a direct call from God."],[2402.92,"But then St."],[2404.0,"Paul would immediately say, and to make sure I didn't get a big head about it."],[2408.98,"I've been beaten, flogged, stoned."],[2412.04,"I've had all of these things that."],[2414.01,"So, you know, God, and both of those St."],[2420.41,"Paul would consider blessings from God."],[2423.37,"St. Paul considered everything he was given by God a blessing, and God giving him those other things to protect him from pride and arrogance."],[2431.21,"That's a blessing, too, from St."],[2433.93,"Paul's perspective. So, yes, it works both ways."],[2442.19,"Because these folks are halfway up the mountain."],[2444.91,"And it's not just Nadab and Abu"],[2450.53,"Most of these elders aren't going to last very many more pages of the Torah either."],[2456.05,"Aaron's going to mess up pretty royally, too."],[2460.93,"It's in not too many chapters."],[2463.83,"So there's a lot of problematic people here."],[2468.0,"But God still reveals himself to them."],[2473.6,"And let me be clear, since I used to use an example, St."],[2476.16,"James, the son of Zebedee is a saint."],[2477.92,"He is not problematic in any way."],[2480.24,"It's just, from our perspective, he didn't have the kind of long ministry that many other figures. had from the apostles"],[2492.76,"Because there's somebody, there's somebody typing an email in the future while they were listening to this."],[2497.96,"And they probably didn't wait until I said that to send me the email complaining."],[2505.56,"Those are my favorite emails, though."],[2508.84,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2516.2,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2521.56,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":20.88,"lv":2,"h":"Where we are in Exodus","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Picking up at beginning of <b>Exodus 24</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Covenant given at Mount Sinai</b> to Israel</li><li class=\"d1\">about to start <b>instructions for building the tabernacle</b> - maybe tonight, \"not good at predicting\"</li><li class=\"d1\">building the tabernacle = <b>most of the rest of Exodus</b></li><li class=\"d0\">So an <b>intermediate period</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Ch. 20: the <b>Ten Commandments</b> - \"the ten words\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Since then: <b>expansions on commandments</b> in practical terms</li><li class=\"d1\">what does it mean to <b>honor the Sabbath</b>? not bear false witness?</li><li class=\"d1\">not steal - other ways to break it than \"this belonged to someone else and I took it\"</li></ul>"},{"t":114.97,"lv":2,"h":"The angel of the Lord, recap","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">End of last time: God telling Moses about the <b>angel of the Lord</b></li><li class=\"d1\">the angel God <b>placed his name in</b></li><li class=\"d1\">= <b>second person of the Trinity</b>, <b>Christ in the Old Testament</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not always \"on camera\" through rest of Torah and Joshua</li><li class=\"d1\">not invisible/appearing - but <b>spoken of directly</b> at several points</li><li class=\"d1\">start of <b>Judges</b>: speaks to Israel, then leaves</li><li class=\"d0\">Period of <b>well over 40 years</b>: angel <b>encamped with Israel</b>, leading them, part of their experience of God</li><li class=\"d0\">End of last reading: angel leads them <b>into the land</b>, helps defeat the <b>giant clans</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Ch. 24 = material <b>between</b> that and <b>ch. 25</b> where tabernacle begins</li></ul>"},{"t":251.67,"lv":2,"h":"Exodus 24:1-2 - Come up, but worship from afar","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">God says to Moses: come up - <b>Aaron, Nadab, Abihu, 70 elders</b>; worship <b>from afar</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Moses alone</b> comes near; <b>people not up at all</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Who is speaking? <b>God</b> - capital H in Orthodox Study Bible</li><li class=\"d0\">Elders + chief priest + his <b>two oldest sons</b> (two senior priests) go <b>partway up</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Top of mountain = where God is; only Moses</li></ul>"},{"t":308.0,"lv":3,"h":"Concentric circles of holiness","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Torah commandments establish <b>concentric circles</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Holy of Holies</b> - where God is</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Holy place</b> - priests offering incense</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Courts</b> - priests and Levites</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Camp</b> - Israelites</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Outside the camp</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Higher holiness the closer you go in</li><li class=\"d0\">Leviticus: <b>only high priest</b> into most holy place, <b>one day a year</b></li><li class=\"d1\">must do much to go in \"safely and not die\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Priests on duty: <b>ritual washings</b>, <b>abstaining/fasting</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Priests and Levites higher than lay people; <b>Israel higher than nations</b> - \"God's people, God dwelling with them\"</li></ul>"},{"t":407.36,"lv":3,"h":"Sinai as the first Holy of Holies","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Already here at Sinai - <b>tabernacle not built yet</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Top of the mountain = Holy of Holies</b> right now</li><li class=\"d0\">Priests and elders <b>near</b> it, can't go <b>into</b> it - only Moses</li><li class=\"d0\">Laity stay at the <b>bottom</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Idea being <b>shown on the mountain</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Tabernacle: system <b>made mobile</b> in the camp, moves with them</li><li class=\"d0\">Later <b>temple</b>: most holy place, holy place, courts, land, then <b>the nations</b></li></ul>"},{"t":473.74,"lv":2,"h":"Exodus 24:3-4 - \"All the words we will do\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Moses tells people <b>all the words and ordinances</b></li><li class=\"d0\">People answer <b>one voice</b>: \"<b>All the words the Lord spoke, we will do</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"good intentions at the time\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Moses <b>writes all the words</b>; rises early</li><li class=\"d0\">Builds <b>altar at foot of mountain</b>, <b>12 stones</b> for 12 tribes</li></ul>"},{"t":515.28,"lv":3,"h":"Moses' authority to write","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Tablets</b> God wrote = Ten Commandments, \"the summary\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Now <b>Moses wrote all the words</b> = the other material we've been reading</li><li class=\"d0\">Not just <b>taking dictation</b></li><li class=\"d1\">invested with authority to <b>apply</b> what God reveals to the people</li><li class=\"d1\">includes authority to <b>put it in writing</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not only adjudicating while alive, then successor, \"whatever Moses said won't matter\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Authority to write for <b>future generations</b> = the <b>Torah</b> in our Bible</li><li class=\"d0\">Authority of Moses isn't just while he's alive</li><li class=\"d0\">Other end of Torah: Moses <b>lays hands on Joshua</b> - what authority passes, what is unique to Moses (later)</li></ul>"},{"t":643.0,"lv":3,"h":"Parallel: apostolic authority","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Crucial for the <b>New Testament</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Apostles' authority not \"while you're alive you're in charge, then somebody else\" - <b>not just bureaucratic church structure</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Unique apostolic authority</b></li><li class=\"d1\">letters to Corinth dealing with local problems = <b>scripture</b>, handed down for generations</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>basis for those who come after</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Like successors of Moses with hands laid on them: take Torah and <b>apply</b> it</li><li class=\"d0\">Apostles' successors <b>don't keep writing Bible</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>apply and interpret</b> apostolic writings and scriptures in later generations</li><li class=\"d0\">Same pattern: Torah ↔ Moses and his successors</li></ul>"},{"t":755.5,"lv":2,"h":"Exodus 24:4-8 - Altar and blood of the covenant","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Altar of <b>12 stones</b>, one per tribe</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Young men</b> offer <b>whole burnt offerings</b> and <b>peace offerings</b> of calves</li><li class=\"d0\">Moses: <b>half the blood in basins</b>, half <b>on the altar</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Reads <b>book of the covenant</b> aloud; people: \"do and be obedient\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Moses <b>sprinkles blood on the people</b>: \"<b>This is the blood of the covenant</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Ritual not set out anywhere yet</li><li class=\"d1\">Leviticus will give sacrifice and blood instructions - \"going on for weeks, you're going to love Bible study\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not told God gave detailed instructions even for altar, place, sacrifices</li><li class=\"d0\">12-stone altar follows <b>Jacob's pattern</b> in Genesis</li><li class=\"d0\">No priesthood yet - <b>not even Aaron</b>; pattern still <b>Abraham, Isaac, Jacob</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"in medias res\"</li></ul>"},{"t":891.75,"lv":3,"h":"Q: Are the 12 pillars standing stones?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: 12 pillars - like <b>standing stones</b>?</li><li class=\"d0\">No - <b>just an altar</b> for sacrificing</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Translation thing</b>: altar made of <b>twelve stones</b></li></ul>"},{"t":920.47,"lv":2,"h":"Blood thrown on people - rare","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Saves <b>half the blood</b>, <b>throws it on the people</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Glad I use water and not blood now\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Very rare</b> in Torah: blood almost never applied to people</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>ordination of the priests</b>: blood on <b>right earlobe, right thumb, right big toe</b> (later)</li><li class=\"d1\">possibly a third - \"I think that is it\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Otherwise blood <b>poured out</b>, or on Day of Atonement applied to <b>inanimate objects</b> to purify - not people</li><li class=\"d0\">Problematic for some views of the <b>atonement</b> - won't delve</li><li class=\"d0\">Talked about in <b>Hebrews</b>: \"without shedding of blood no remission\" - usual interpretation doesn't fit Torah</li><li class=\"d0\">Most people in Israel's history: <b>\"99.99999%\"</b> never had blood on them</li></ul>"},{"t":1061.6,"lv":2,"h":"Q: Same as Abraham's covenant?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: related to <b>covenant with Abraham</b>? a new covenant?</li><li class=\"d0\">Abraham: <b>animals split in half</b>, \"butterflied\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>oath-taking ritual</b>: walk between halves = \"may I end up like these animals\"</li><li class=\"d1\">in Genesis <b>God's presence as fiery torch</b> moves between the halves</li><li class=\"d1\">God, not Abraham, swears: \"if I don't keep my promises, may I end up like these\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Same here: <b>people taking an oath</b> - \"we got this\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Blood of the sacrifice thrown on them</b> to \"seal the deal\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Shed blood implies <b>consequence of violating</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>witness</b> to what you swore, <b>against you</b> if you violate</li></ul>"},{"t":1198.07,"lv":2,"h":"Blood of the covenant at the Last Supper","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"This is the <b>blood of the covenant</b>\" - looks similar</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Matthew, Mark, Luke</b> describe the <b>mystical supper</b>, Christ instituting the <b>Eucharist</b>; <b>John</b> doesn't</li><li class=\"d0\">Fourth place: <b>1 Corinthians</b>, Paul</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Matthew</b> makes a special point, follows up later</li><li class=\"d0\">Christ on the cup: \"<b>my blood of the new covenant</b>, shed for you and for many\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Sacrifice that initiates the Mosaic covenant</b> ↔ Christ's</li></ul>"},{"t":1265.64,"lv":3,"h":"\"New\" covenant means renewed","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Jeremiah 31</b> (Hebrew numbering) and others: <b>new covenant</b> with Israel in the latter days</li><li class=\"d0\">Greek <i>kainē</i> = <b>renewed, refreshed</b>, not \"never existed before\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Parallel: <b>1 John</b> - \"a new commandment: love one another\"</li><li class=\"d1\">but it's all through the Bible - <b>love your enemies</b> a chapter ago in Exodus</li><li class=\"d1\">John: \"not a new commandment... from the beginning\" → <b>renewing</b>, \"let me remind you\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Jeremiah 31: first thing = God will <b>write the Torah on hearts</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Torah = the \"old covenant\"</li><li class=\"d1\">new = old one <b>written on your heart</b> → <b>renewed, transformed</b>, same thing</li><li class=\"d0\">Greek Jeremiah <b>rearranged</b> from Hebrew - more at Jeremiah</li><li class=\"d0\">Christ: new covenant in his blood = <b>prophesied covenant</b> being renewed; his <b>self-offering</b> initiates it</li><li class=\"d0\">People at Sinai: <b>vowed</b>, then <b>sprinkled</b> → participants</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>eat Christ's flesh, drink his blood</b> (<b>John 6</b>) → participant in new covenant</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Eucharist</b> = <b>renewing the vow</b> to Christ</li><li class=\"d1\">\"renewed a lot because we mess up\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not professing we've done it perfectly - <b>recommitting</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1586.37,"lv":2,"h":"\"His blood be on us\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Matthew: soon after, crowd: \"<b>Let his blood be on us and on our children</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Does <b>not</b> mean Jewish people guilty of Jesus' death for eternity</li><li class=\"d0\">Gospels pattern: someone says something and <b>doesn't realize what they're saying</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Caiaphas</b>: \"good for one man to die\" - meant <b>get the Romans off our backs</b>; words far more profound</li><li class=\"d0\">Crowd just wants Jesus dead, but really saying they want to be <b>part of the new covenant</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Almost another time blood is applied to people\" - clear <b>reference back</b> to this</li><li class=\"d0\">Matthew's pattern</li><li class=\"d1\">Jesus' murder: <b>innocent</b>, hideous execution</li><li class=\"d1\">but <b>God takes that human evil and turns it to great good</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not blaming anyone - God turned the crime into a <b>blessing for the Jewish people and all nations</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Contrast: they say \"we'll do everything\" - and this group <b>all dies in the desert</b>; \"complete inverse\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Christ/Matthew alluding back to this episode - blood doesn't go on people otherwise</li></ul>"},{"t":1785.54,"lv":2,"h":"Exodus 24:9-11 - They saw God and ate and drank","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Moses, Aaron, Nadab, Abihu, <b>70 elders</b> go up</li><li class=\"d0\">See \"the place where God stood\"</li><li class=\"d1\">under his feet <b>paved work of sapphire</b>, like the <b>firmament</b> in purity</li><li class=\"d1\">= <b>God standing on the sky</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Of Israel's chosen men, not one was missing\"</li><li class=\"d0\">They saw God and <b>ate and drank</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>God in human form</b> - \"he's got feet\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Meal with God</b> right after the <b>sacrifice and blood of the covenant</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"Mystical supper. Do you see things coming together?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Christ eating the meal and appealing back to this chapter \"not for nothing\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1873.85,"lv":2,"h":"Why Nadab and Abihu?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">What's coming in <b>Leviticus 9-10</b>: <b>Nadab and Abihu die</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>two oldest sons of Aaron</b>; younger sons, <b>Eleazar</b>, become high priest</li><li class=\"d1\">almost the next story if you skip tabernacle instructions/building</li><li class=\"d0\">Q: why are they given this vision?</li><li class=\"d1\">could have been Aaron and all four sons</li><li class=\"d0\">\"The <b>question</b> is important, not the answer\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Echoes through <b>OT and NT</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1969.44,"lv":3,"h":"The same question across Scripture","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">OT: why bring <b>12 tribes</b> out of Egypt and settle them when <b>10 will go</b>?</li><li class=\"d1\">God knows what will happen</li><li class=\"d0\">NT: Christ has the <b>twelve</b> - <b>Judas</b> among them</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Inner circle of three</b>: <b>Peter, James, John</b></li><li class=\"d1\">raising the dead</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Transfiguration</b> - \"about to celebrate as we record this\"</li><li class=\"d1\">other times aside to pray</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Galatians</b>: Paul's <b>pillars</b> - Peter, James, John</li><li class=\"d1\">different James = <b>the Lord's brother</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>James son of Zebedee</b> killed by <b>Herod</b> early in Acts, never really led the church</li><li class=\"d0\">So why him in the inner circle? Why not someone else?</li><li class=\"d0\">Found all through scripture: God <b>chooses to reveal himself to some and not others</b>, at different levels</li><li class=\"d0\">No answer other than he reveals himself to different people at different times</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Surely a better 12th guy than Judas\" - <b>Andrew</b>?</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Surely people as faithful as <b>Judah and Benjamin</b>\" over the \"no good northern tribes\"</li><li class=\"d0\">God knowing how someone will react <b>doesn't stop him giving the light</b></li><li class=\"d1\">doesn't give only to those who respond best or have a \"magnificent destiny\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"just not how God works\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2220.72,"lv":2,"h":"Asking it selfishly","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">We ask from a <b>selfish perspective</b></li><li class=\"d1\">like <b>James and John (and their mother)</b> wanting right and left hand, other disciples indignant</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Why did God give this to that person? Why hasn't he done that for me?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Rarely \"why has God given me blessings I didn't deserve?\" - \"which we should think more often\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Focus on those we <b>haven't been given</b>, especially if given to someone we don't like or think wastes it</li><li class=\"d0\">Receiving a blessing or revelation → <b>not special and wonderful</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Nadab and Abihu</b> eating and drinking had no reason to think God loved them more than those at the foot</li><li class=\"d1\">or to be jealous of Moses going further</li></ul>"},{"t":2357.39,"lv":3,"h":"Fathers on visions; Paul's thorn","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Fathers: if you think you have a <b>vision</b> or an <b>angel appeared</b> → always <b>assume no</b></li><li class=\"d1\">if real, God will make it <b>so real you can't deny it</b></li><li class=\"d1\">until then <b>doubt it</b> - other way lies <b>pride</b>, \"I'm the one God has chosen\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Paul's thorn in the flesh</b>, hardships</li><li class=\"d1\">knew <b>direct call from God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">immediately: <b>beaten, flogged, stoned</b> - keeps him from a big head</li><li class=\"d1\">both = <b>blessings</b>; the hardships protect from <b>pride and arrogance</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"It works both ways\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2442.19,"lv":2,"h":"Problematic people still see God","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Folks halfway up the mountain - not just Nadab and Abihu</li><li class=\"d0\">Most of the elders won't last many more pages of Torah</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Aaron</b> will \"mess up pretty royally\" - not many chapters away</li><li class=\"d0\">Lots of problematic people, yet <b>God still reveals himself</b> to them</li><li class=\"d0\">Clarify: <b>St James son of Zebedee is a saint</b>, not problematic - just a short ministry from our perspective</li><li class=\"d0\">Joke: someone emailing complaint \"before I said that\" - \"my favorite emails\"</li></ul>"}]});
